{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922136-adapting-the-scp-foundation-s-groups-of-interest-to-cofd","id":922136,"title":"Adapting The SCP Foundation's Groups Of Interest To CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-27T12:00:37-07:00","id":922136,"title":"Adapting The SCP Foundation's Groups Of Interest To CofD","content":"<a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/groups-of-interest\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Here is the list.</b></a> These groups and their associated SCPs are amazing inspirational material for Hunter, Mage, Demon and probably Deviant. However, I'm interested not only in alternate interpretations for the other gamelines, but also in actual storytelling hints and plot hooks in general. It would cheapen their appeal if there was only one version or explanation for each one. Ideas for interactions with mortals are also welcome.<br /> <br /> From what I've read, it seems the scientific and hoarder aspects of the Foundation itself could be incorporated into a division of Task Force VALKYRIE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:25:37-07:00","id":922190,"title":"","content":"I've always thought Doctor Wondertainment was a crazy mage that was doing experiments on how to get around the sleeper's inability to remember magic or possibly a mortal magician thats a genuis in several different forms of non supernal magic. <br /> <br /> The Factory is what happens when a Abyssal verge and a God machine infrastructure collide. So any time a group of mages go investigate God machine infrastructure if that preform enough magic that a crap ton of paradox occurs the abyss and god machine mash together to create a twisted Factory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T18:04:45-07:00","id":922952,"title":"","content":"Considering their vast resources, bastard coated in bastard inclinations, and inquisitive nature, I'd make them a Seers of the Throne project- saving the world, and solving mysteries, but it's not like they care if people get hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T21:06:28-07:00","id":923047,"title":"","content":"I've used them as the Cheiron Group.<br /> <br /> Let me find the one that's most shocking, IMO. I always forget the number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T21:08:23-07:00","id":923049,"title":"","content":"That actually didn't take me as long as I'd thought it would.<br /> <br /> TW: basically everything? It's so unclear because of how much is redacted. <br /> <br /> Off my interpretation, TW: CSA and torture to a child<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/nav:side/social-facebook.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231\" target=\"_blank\"> SCP-231 - SCP Foundation </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The SCP Foundation's 'top-secret' archives, declassified for your enjoyment. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:08:49-07:00","id":923331,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3093_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3093\" data-vbnamecard=\"3093\">hm8453a</a>, I'd appreciate it if the discussion didn't focus on that SCP. There's this Tale with an alternate take on it which I prefer, but I digress.<br /> <br /> My favorite GoI is easily Dr. Wondertainment. I once thought there was a fae being of some kind behind the designs of the toys and the weird legalese, but the more I think about it, the more I like the interpretation that Wondertainment is actually a legacy of Immortals. This would explain the shifts in design that the company's toys undergo sometimes. If the owner was a Mage or a Genius, they'd have to deal with Quiescence/Dissonance/Paradox or Havoc, repectively. There's also something very empathic in how fun the toys sound, and many fae don't have a lot of empathy or creativity.<br /> <br /> So, which interpretation do you all lean toward? Excentric and Intellectually gifted mortals working together as a loose corporation with anomalous resources, or an alien intelligence who lives inside each toy and doesn't understand that its creations might harm us?<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, if we're using Werewolf terms, Dr. Wondertainment might be a whimsical Idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:17:25-07:00","id":923376,"title":"","content":"Also, the Church Of The Broken God and its sub-sects works perfectly as a large scale God-Machine Cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:57:25-07:00","id":923626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922136-adapting-the-scp-foundation-s-groups-of-interest-to-cofd?p=923331#post923331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3093_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3093\" data-vbnamecard=\"3093\">hm8453a</a>, I'd appreciate it if the discussion didn't focus on that SCP. There's this Tale with an alternate take on it which I prefer, but I digress.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so sorry! Totally, I apologize. <br /> <br /> Anyway. Moving on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T08:04:43-07:00","id":928136,"title":"","content":"Alexylva University is explicitly mentioned as being in a universe where the Roman Empire persisted into the modern age- and apparently reaches as far as the American South. The University also sends highly advanced technology that basically amount to toys in their world through a teleport to our world to make an inter-universal black market. There's also hints that our universe would've followed the same route if not for the interference of an unknown party. <br /> <br /> The unknown party just has to be the God-Machine. Which could make Alexylva University infrastructure or some sort of God-Machine cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T01:54:54-07:00","id":928647,"title":"","content":"Everything SCP has makes for delicious WoD fodder, as long as you figure out how to port it into the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:51:07-07:00","id":928817,"title":"","content":"I always liked the Sarkic cults-it's that strange balance between eldritch horror, biological tinkering, and high-fantasy caliber evil sorcery. I really loved the fiction about a family line of Mekhanist &quot;werewolves&quot; pursuing a decades-long war with a particular Karcist shepherd defiling their lands. It's that mix of humanistic dark fantasy and borderline cosmic body horror that really gets me.<br /> <br /> They seem like a pretty clear example of what Abyssal or Lower Depths cultists should look like-alien in form, but almost obscenely base and human in motive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:55:17-07:00","id":928819,"title":"","content":"What about Hermann Fuller's Circus Of The Disquieting? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>, didn't you adapt some poison-eating, masquerade-hating circus freaks from GURPS that might start such an organization?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T11:11:48-07:00","id":928823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922136-adapting-the-scp-foundation-s-groups-of-interest-to-cofd?p=928819#post928819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Hermann Fuller's Circus Of The Disquieting? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>, didn't you adapt some poison-eating, masquerade-hating circus freaks from GURPS that might start such an organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I would be working on finishing the latest GURPS conversion, were it not for cram school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T13:07:32-07:00","id":928879,"title":"","content":"Of course, one of the major differences to consider is that the Foundation has essentially limitless funding and influence. They can pretty much tell any government anywhere &quot;do this&quot;, and it's done- and they pretty much need it, because a lot of things they deal with pose large-scale threats to humanity, earth, reality itself, etc. <br /> <br /> In ChroD, on the other hand, all of the Hunter groups are massively less powerful, and even TFV and Cheiron can't order around governments and have funding problems. But the world hasn't ended, partially because the supernatural forces aren't generally as powerful, but more because, unlike in the SCP universe, they're primarily made up of groups of sapient beings that largely police themselves. <br /> <br /> I've found that the best things to yank are individual SCPs and groups other than the Foundation, rather than trying to port the whole atmosphere. Though the Foundation can be a source of inspiration, since its methods provide examples of taking on the supernatural with (mostly) mundane technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T15:05:24-07:00","id":929987,"title":"","content":"Everyone, you seem to have forgotten the most important GOI:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BhssrYohwaw\" data-code=\"BhssrYohwaw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/BhssrYohwaw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> More seriously, AWCY are Mages. And Eric is clearly an Archmaster (or have they gotten rid of all mentions of Eric?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:34:55-07:00","id":930085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of